"He was a dwarf, he was a wolf, he was a cockatrice, he was a demigod..."

This is my 2. ascension and even feels better than my first one: It's a
genoless! As a sidenote, I don't count my very first one, where I escaped
in celestial disgrace (however, from a point of experience it was, but
otherwise just an *escape*, not an ascension).

After playing almost always wizards, I was looking for something new and
challenging this time and so I started a couple of (hum neu) arcs. Every
game was as short as interesting and after killing 15 human arcs in a row
I decided to try a lawful (<- no choice) dwarf. That was even more
challenging, since all of my previous wizards either where neutral or
chaotic. An additional challenge was to play the whole game in tty on
Linux console, where I was used to play tile versions before. This turned
out to be a bit tricky in Sokoban, with the result of 2 minor and one
major mistake (had to destroy a boulder). As a last sidenote: Quaffing
from unid'd potions was something I introduced in my games with the 15
unlucky arcs before. None of them were killed as a direct or indirect
result from quaffing a potion...

And here we go:

Rubinstein started on new moon, but (or because?) he was covered by an
everlasting aura, which seemed to protect him even against the most stupid
mistakes from his mentor. The first item he found was a !PoI. Being
permanently invisible in the early game, together with the arc's natural
speed, surely was a nice advantage. But the RNG didn't wait long to
present the bill in form of 3 shops in a row and, of course, no mummy
(-wrapping) around. Went down to the mines and found a BoH, what naturally
means that Sokoban contains another one, and so it was. Finally found a
mummy wrapping, but a cursed one. Hoping that one of the shops would
provide some useful stuff to get rid of it again, Rubinstein put it on,
being visible for a longer time now (no, the shops didn't have any scrolls
of destroy armor or remove curse).

The first serious incident happened on Dlvl 5: Got lycanthropy! No
wolfesbane around, no altar to check prayer timeout (had to pray already
before). Summed up 6 friends and actually had some fun with wolfish hunter
technics. Although wolves seem to be less strong than large dogs, they
seem to act in a more 'intelligent' way: No heroic kamikaze attacks but
well organised teamwork. This little episode wasn't too bad at all (I
seriously was thinking about ascending a wolf sometime!).

Deep below the Minetown he finally found a luckstone. Some scary moments
here, after loosing some vital stuff to a nymph: BoH, mattock, dwarvish
mithril coat. Fortunately one of the two remaining wolf pets was turned
into a gray dragon meanwhile (from one of the countless polytraps) and
solved the problem.

Up again in the main dungeon, he found his first coaligned altar on Dlvl
11. First gift was Snickersnee. Don't know why so many people turn their
nose against Snickersnee: I was under the impression that it is clearly
better, even unenchanted, than the +2 mattock, but maybe it's weak only
compared to other artifact-weapons... While praying on the altar for some
holy water, he got his second 'gift': "You are the Hand of Elbereth" which
gave him 2 missing intrinsics (never got sleep resistance from elven
corpses).

One level below, on Dlvl 12, there was a big room with the portal to Lord
Carnarvon, but Rubinstein was still at Xp 12. Carefully explored a few
levels below, found a !PoGL, got Excalibur (from a fountain), found a
=RoC, speed boots and finally reached Xp 14. Before he went to the
college, he had to deal with a couple of serious mistakes. The misery
began with a deep fall through a trapdoor, from which he nearly lost his
pet. He had to realise, that controlled level-teleport with reading a ?SoT
while confused, doesn't work w/o intrinsic teleport (or a =RoT). Thus he
deliberately got teleportitis, only to realise now, that it doesn't work
yet w/o teleport control! Although he got a =RoTC later from the castle
wand, he never got rid of teleportitis again, not even after eating every
tengu, that came along (not recommended for lawful dwarfes: All tengus
were generated peaceful).

Nevertheless, time for the quest, even with teleportitis...

Never had to fight the Minion of Huhetotl before, but a tame gray dragon,
a =RoC and Excalibur seems to be a fearsome setup and thus he fell soon
after an unsuccessful attempt to escape upstairs. Another first-timer:
Just before Huhetotl appeared in front of Rubinstein, he found a silver
saber and immediatly switched to #twoweapon (never did before, no wonder,
as wizard). Even unskilled the effect was impressive!

On Dlvl 22 another big mistake, as a follow-up from the previous. While
still searching for a =RoTC, he put on an unid'd ring, tested for TC
(negativ) and just forgot to remove it again! What now follows is already
told in "My current game is a nightmare!" (polymorphing into a
cockatrice):

<pan.2003.07.07.05.44.21.950327@lasker.fqdn.th-h.de>

When entering Medusa's level (Dlvl 23) he still had no means of
levitation, thus he digged down and took her from below (hope this doesn't
sound indecently in english translation). Smashing some statues here
reminded him of arcs being restricted in abusing statues (never destroyed
the Oracle statues, though), but with a blessed luckstone a little penalty
shouldn't hurt too much.

The Castle was on Dlvl 25. No music instrument this time (i like the
'master mind' method). Had to zap the drawbridge and later freeze the moat
with a /WoCold, not a great deal at all with a =RoC. While sitting in
front of the /WoW, going genoless was already decided, but I needed a full
hour to decide *not* to go wishless, too. "But hey, it's just your first
arc on your second ascension, don't be crazy!" I told to myself and got a
0:1 wand, fortunately wished for 2 b?SoC (got only 1) and used up all 3
remaining wishes at once: +2 SDSM (got +0), =RoTC (finally!) and a +BoID
(Nr.1 on my favourite-items-list, can't live without it). A magic marker
or a =RoFA probably would have been the wiser decision...

The throne doesn't grant him a wish as none of all 3 thrones in the game
did. Found speed boots (Nr.2 of my favourites) and a "AoMB". The latter
was both his 'virtuel' AoLS* and tinning kit in one and never was removed
again. Was using a magig lamp as light source until the end, got one wish
from a fountain but still wonder where the 6th wish came from...

*being drowned (in water, not in booze) is what a dwarf fears more than
death...

Arch-liches and master mind flayers always where my most feared opponents
and so I felt a bit uneasy, when an arch-lich said hallo right after
entrance into Gehennom. Dunno, maybe they respect brute force more than
magic or was it Rubinstein's relative low Xp? Three hits usually were
enough to turn them into clouds of smoke and dust, no time to cast any
tricky stuff this time...

Not so the mind flayers: The first encounter with a MF used up all the
grease from Rubinstein's helm. Unfortunately the can of grease only had 1
portion left and a terrible typo made the can greasing itself - what a
waste! So he still had to be extremely careful, especially with MMFs.

Joined Juiblex on Dlvl 32, while levitating: You hit Juiblex!  The silver
sears Juiblex's flesh!  You kill Juiblex! Here you can see Rubinstein
affectionately kissing his silver saber...

The next canditates - Asmodeus, Baalzebub, Orcus - were all treated in
the same manner: One down and never come back...

Baalzebub (Dlvl 33): Status of Baalzebub (lawful):

Level 41  HP 166(166)  AC -5, invisible. (He really should read r.g.r.n
and work out his AC next time)

Alert: MMF on Dlvl 34 (seen with telepathy). Let him alone for now...

Dlvl 38: Orcus-town

Found another ring of levitation and the first magic marker here. 49
charges, used up for ?SoEA, ?SoEW and a ?SoC. Blessed the latter and got
50 new charges.

Another arch-lich on Dlvl 43 and, finally, the 

VS on Dlvl 45.

The candles still were in Izchak's shop (bad experience from an unlucky
barbarian). Had to prepare the retreat for the final run anyway and took
the opportunity for a short visit in Vlad's tower.

Back to the ground (with candles now) and up again, Rubinstein needed some
time to find the right entrance to the Wizard's Tower, but finally fought
his way up to those blown up, impudent wizard called 'Yendor', showed him
his finger, err, /WoD and let the =RoC do the rest. One of the last
remaining critters was a cockatrice...

Back to the VS with the Book and a 0:2 Bell (another typo), Rubinstein
didn't remember the correct sequence of the ritual and wasted another
charge from the Bell (+ an 'invocation' of some vampire lords, a lich,
etc.). With the last charge of the Bell and a dwarven grumbling about "all
that intellectual stuff" he finally got in and could do what a dwarf is
born to do (we leave out any details here, in case of children could read
this).

The final run

Rubinstein was bothered 3 times only from the Wizard on his way back to
Dlvl 1. Never used the /WoD on the wizard anymore, whacked him 'handmade'.
Was thrown back 2 times only, but with several 'malignant aura'. Some
b?SoRC saved the day...

As one of the last actions in his mortal form Rubinstein polypiled some
spare unicorn horns: 2 cans of grease and 2 magic whistles (never found
one, nearly useless now, except for the angel on astral plane). 

Actually this was the last mistake: Why not polypile the remaining useless
rings? Rubinstein was going to ascend genoless *and* =RoFA-less...

Arrived on Dlvl 1 he picked up a stored 5:0 crystal ball and proceeded to
the planes.

The Elemental Planes

Plane of Earth

Just whacked the Wizard once again, when real life knocked on the door: PC
crashed! (it's summertime, the usual hardware heat problem)

Fortunately 'recover' worked, but not as expected back to DLvl 1, but on
the Plane of Earth, as arrived before on the portal (always thought,
'recover' brings you back to the last level *before* the crash) including
the wizard! Well, no problem, the Wizard couldn't know what would happen
now, but Rubinstein knew...

The crystal ball showed the next portal not far away and after 2 zaps from
a /WoDig Rubinstein finally could drop a huge stock of wands...

Plane or Air

The crystal ball revealed the next portal on the opposite side of the
planes and it's major drawback: It's just too heavy and was the reason for
being engulfed once by an air element. Once the ball was packed into the
BoH again, Rubinstein was able to reach the other side, carefully
preventing any unnecessary fights.

Plane of Fire

Rubinstein had to 'work' a bit here, before he could use the ball.
Allthough the crystal ball was blessed, one charge failed, but the next
one showed the portal, not far away from the entrance again.

Plane of Water

The crystal ball was pretty useless here, since the portal moves around,
but finally he reached the...

Astral Plane

A friendly guardian Angel of Quetzalcoatl offered assistance to Rubinstein
and 2 athame (one of them was +3!) on the floor showed the direction: He
picked up one and engraved the E-Word wherever he could. An inner voice
whispered to him "go left"...

When he finally opened the first door, a dreadful creature appeared: DEATH
himself! At this point Rubinstein had to learn the real meaning of 'frozen
to death' and while he regretted the absence of a =RoFA, DEATH slowly took
about 50 HP from the helpless poor Rubinstein. But even this horror show
finally passed, and now it was DEATH's turn to learn a lesson: Material
rules!

After this problem was solved, there still was another one: An abnormal
traffic here! Priests and angels, bugs and spiders, lost adventurers (Eve
the Rover, Stephen the Voyager) and countless other critters made any
movement extremely difficult, if not impossible. Nevertheless, the newly
created magic whistles came in handy here and so he was able to free his
assisting angel from even more trouble at least...

Moving forward in super-slow-motion, they finally reached the temple
entrance. After a last 'E-Word' to keep the majority of the critters
outside, they were greeted by an impatient priest: Here you are, finally!
What have you done all the time? Come on, you know, what to do now!

Rubinstein went to the altar, took the angel close to his side, and:



